Read @include / -i libraries from the binary's embedded share/awk tree.

UNPIN_AWKLIB_DIR (set by the build) is the mount: it ends every AWKPATH,
the default one being "." and nothing else, so the embedded libraries are
found even when the user sets AWKPATH and a library of theirs still wins.
The library search (do_find_source) stats through unpin-vfs, and srcopen
opens an embedded library through it; a program file given with -f stays
on gawk's own devopen. Embedded files all stat with inode 0, so
files_are_same compares their names to tell two libraries apart.

